<title>UK: Invesco restructures non-U.S. operations.</title>
<headline>Invesco restructures non-U.S. operations.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment namagement company Invesco Plc said on Friday that, following its recent merger with AIM Management, it will consolidate its non-U.S. operations in a new Global Division.</p>
<p>This will include the Pacific and European regions and will be headed by Invesco board member Michael Benson.</p>
<p>Following the merger, the combined group is to be known as Amvesco and will have around $150 billion under management.</p>
<p>Reporting to Benson, will be Tristan Hillgarth who has been appointed chief executive of the Europe region.</p>
<p>Invesco also said that Norman Riddell will be leaving its board at the end of 1996. Riddell has been in charge of Invesco's UK operations. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
